Ladybird exposes block as the computed display of a block button. Its
button layout already establishes a block formatting context. Blink’s
HTMLButtonElement::CreateLayoutObject chooses a LayoutBlockFlow for an
ordinary block button. Gecko’s nsCSSFrameConstructor::FindHTMLButtonData
selects the button’s frame, and WebKit’s RenderTheme::adjustStyle
retains block for this case.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 returned block
for an explicitly block button and retained flex and grid for those
displays. For a text input with an explicit inline display, Chrome and
WebKit returned inline-block, as Ladybird does. Firefox returned inline.
